# fixedbugs, defect 2650, 2026-11-21: a generic, `same`, at a case of each of
# two variants of one name, `Token.num` here and in `other`. A case put its
# variant in no set, so the key was the rendering `Token.num` alone, and the
# two instances were one C function, which clang refused at exit 2.
#
# The cause, for every case of defect 2650: a synthetic C name was the hash
# of the type's rendering, which writes no module, and of the sorted set of the
# declared types it names, the same set either way round. Where that set does
# not tell which declaration each name stands for, the key also carries those
# declarations in the rendering's order (`selfhost/emit/synth_places.hero`).
use other

variant Token
    num
        v: i64

function same<T>(x: T) -> T
    return x

function mine(t: Token) -> i64
    return match t
        .num n => same(n).v

function theirs(t: other.Token) -> i64
    return match t
        .num n => same(n).v * 10

function main()
    print(mine(.num(v: 1)) + theirs(.num(v: 2)))
